Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0021 + 0023-0032 (touches nvidia/dspark.py
only). VLLM_DSPARK_CONTEXT_KV_GROUPED=1 (default off; needs the vllm_exl3_moe plugin with EXL3 draft layers): DSpark's
context KV (precompute_and_store_context_kv) computes every draft layer's wkv on the projected target hidden in one
EXL3 launch (vllm_exl3_moe.dense.context_kv_group, the wkv part of each layer's fused wq_a|wkv as one exl3_mrow group)
at <= 16 rows. Today each of the three layers runs its whole fused wq_a|wkv (5.7 MB at K5) and drops the wq_a columns:
17 MB read for 4.9 MB used, three ~30 us launches a round (Oct 21 prose trace). Any other case keeps the loop. A
drafter-only, rounding-class change (the group splits K differently from the fused launch): the target's outputs are
untouched, so greedy text is identical and only acceptance can move. Test: plugin tests/test_dense_gpu.py
test_context_kv_group (serve image, GPU).

